{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.StandardModel.SecondCrossingInvariant","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.StandardModel.SecondCrossingInvariant","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Groupoid","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Rat.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.SecondCrossingInvariant.exists_writhe_degenerate_pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.SecondCrossingInvariant.exists_writhe_degenerate_pair","kind":"theorem","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/SecondCrossingInvariant.lean#L198-L210","doc":"**(Conditional on `SecondCrossingInvariant`.)** Any second crossing\ninvariant forces a writhe-degenerate pair separated by the hypercharge\n`Y = a·w + b·B`.  Proved from the reduction lemma; the only unproved input\nis the class instance (§3b-cond).  This checks the conjecture is *coherent*:\nits hypotheses genuinely deliver the object the `HyperchargeInvariant`\nconjecture demands. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.SecondCrossingInvariant.exists_second_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.SecondCrossingInvariant.exists_second_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/SecondCrossingInvariant.lean#L190-L190","doc":"There is an integer-valued gauge-invariant second invariant `B`\n(intended: Milnor `μ̄₁₂₃`, an integer because the Borromean pairwise\nlinkings vanish) and integers `a, b` with `b ≠ 0` such that\n`Y = a·w + b·B` realizes Gell-Mann–Nishijima `Q = I₃ + Y/2`, with `I₃`\nthe writhe reading `w/2`, and does **not** factor through the writhe. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.SecondCrossingInvariant.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.SecondCrossingInvariant.mk","kind":"ctor","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/SecondCrossingInvariant.lean#L183-L183","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.SecondCrossingInvariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.SecondCrossingInvariant","kind":"class","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/SecondCrossingInvariant.lean#L164-L196","doc":"**Conjecture class (primary): the second crossing invariant.**  Over a\ngroupoid `S` of topological states with a derived charge `Q`, the writhe\nreading `I₃` and the writhe `w`, there is an integer-valued gauge-invariant\n**second invariant `B`** (intended: the Milnor triple linking `μ̄₁₂₃` of the\nthree color-tube components) and integers `a, b` with `b ≠ 0` such that the\nweak hypercharge\n\n  `Y = a·w + b·B`\n\nis a genuine ℤ-linear combination (the `b·B` piece is present) realizing\nGell-Mann–Nishijima `Q = I₃ + Y/2`, and — the sharp clause — `Y` does\n**not** factor through the writhe.\n\nIntended instantiation: `S` = knot-state groupoid; `Q = w/2` the Coulomb\ncharge, `I₃ = w/2` the writhe reading (both 2026-06-02 audit), `B = μ̄₁₂₃`\nthe Borromean baryon-number invariant, `a = 0`, `b = 1` (so `Y = B`) on the\nnon-strange sector.  **Open:** no instance — the identification `B = μ̄₁₂₃`,\nits GMN normalization, and the strangeness/`sin²θ_W` extension are not\nderived. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.writheZero_Y_eq_twoQ_rat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.writheZero_Y_eq_twoQ_rat","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/SecondCrossingInvariant.lean#L150-L162","doc":"The rational statement is recovered from the cleared one: over `ℚ` the\nfamiliar `I₃ = w/2`, `Q = I₃ + Y/2` hypotheses imply the cleared ones, so\nno content is lost by generalising. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.writheZero_Y_eq_twoQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.writheZero_Y_eq_twoQ","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/SecondCrossingInvariant.lean#L127-L148","doc":"**Writhe-`0` sector lemma (proved).** On any state whose writhe is `0`\n(the Borromean baryon, per the s5-so3 audit), the writhe reading\n`I₃ = w/2` vanishes, so Gell-Mann–Nishijima forces `Y = 2Q`: the *entire*\nhypercharge is carried by the second invariant, not the writhe.  This is\nthe sharp reason the writhe alone cannot supply `Y` on the baryon.\n\nStated in **cleared (division-free)** form -- `2·I₃ = w` and\n`2Q = 2I₃ + Y` rather than `I₃ = w/2` and `Q = I₃ + Y/2` -- so it holds over\nan arbitrary `CommRing R` with **no characteristic hypothesis**.  Note the\nproof never needs `I₃ X = 0`, only `2·I₃ X = 0`, which is why no invertible\n`2` is required.  Matches the formulation in\n`QOU/StandardModel/HyperchargeBatteryReduction.lean`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.baryon_vacuum_separating","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.baryon_vacuum_separating","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/SecondCrossingInvariant.lean#L113-L125","doc":"**Concrete Borromean/vacuum separating pair (proved).** The canonical\nbaryon (`w = 0`, `B = 1`: Borromean triple linking `μ̄₁₂₃ = 1`) and the\nvacuum/meson (`w = 0`, `B = 0`: no triple) are a writhe-degenerate pair\nseparated by the second invariant.  This realizes, with the framework's own\nobjects, the pair whose *existence* the hypercharge conjecture asserts. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.secondInvariant_gives_separating_pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.secondInvariant_gives_separating_pair","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/SecondCrossingInvariant.lean#L93-L111","doc":"**Reduction lemma (proved).** If a candidate invariant `B` does *not*\nfactor through the writhe `w`, then there is a **writhe-degenerate pair**\nof states — equal writhe, distinct `B` — exactly the object the\nhypercharge conjecture requires.  This is the constructive converse of\n`HyperchargeInvariant.exists_writhe_degenerate_pair`: a genuine second\ninvariant automatically discharges the non-factorization clause. ","signatureChunk":0}]}